    "thisYear": 145957596,
    "lastYear": 122000000,
    "tenYearAvg": 105000000,
    "note": "It's official: Spider-Man: Brand New Day's Monday actuals confirmed $360.1M — the new all-time domestic opening-weekend record, dethroning Avengers: Endgame's $357.1M mark from 2019 after seven years. Global landed at $932M (Endgame still holds the worldwide opening record at $1.22B). Brand New Day also grabbed the all-time single-day ($169.8M Friday w/ previews) and preview ($72M) records along the way. The Odyssey held at #2 with a final $51.0M third weekend, pushing it to $395.6M domestic and roughly $910M worldwide. Combined, the two delivered the biggest box-office weekend in history at an estimated $430M+ overall."
  },
